# ParticleSoundSim scene
# Seam-leak test: the 4 x 7 x 3 m wood shoebox with each face split into
# two triangles (12 planes). Total energy and T30 should match
# shoebox_4x7x3_wood.pss within ~1%; particles escaping through the
# diagonal seams would show up as lower energy / shorter decay.
pss 1

# each quad (v0 v1 v2 v3) is split into (v0 v1 v2) and (v0 v2 v3),
# which keeps the CCW-from-inside winding
plane wood 3   -2 -3.5 0    2 -3.5 0    2  3.5 0     # floor
plane wood 3   -2 -3.5 0    2  3.5 0   -2  3.5 0
plane wood 3   -2 -3.5 3   -2  3.5 3    2  3.5 3     # ceiling
plane wood 3   -2 -3.5 3    2  3.5 3    2 -3.5 3
plane wood 3   -2 -3.5 0   -2  3.5 0   -2  3.5 3     # wall x=-2
plane wood 3   -2 -3.5 0   -2  3.5 3   -2 -3.5 3
plane wood 3    2 -3.5 0    2 -3.5 3    2  3.5 3     # wall x=+2
plane wood 3    2 -3.5 0    2  3.5 3    2  3.5 0
plane wood 3   -2 -3.5 0   -2 -3.5 3    2 -3.5 3     # wall y=-3.5
plane wood 3   -2 -3.5 0    2 -3.5 3    2 -3.5 0
plane wood 3   -2  3.5 0    2  3.5 0    2  3.5 3     # wall y=+3.5
plane wood 3   -2  3.5 0    2  3.5 3   -2  3.5 3

emitter -0.4  2.1 0.75  power_db 70 70 70 70 70 70 70 70
emitter  0.4 -2.1 0.75  power_db 75 75 75 75 75 75 75 75

receiver -0.24 -0.56 0.6 0.5
